    "show_share": true,
    "description": "In a powerful analysis, Zulfiqar A. Bhutta, Director of the Institute for Global Health and Development (IGHD) at Aga Khan University, and his colleagues have called for renewed global attention to the plight of children in conflict zones. Their analysis, titled  \"When is enough, enough? Humanitarian rights and protection for children in conflict settings must be revisited,\"  emphasizes the need for changes to international rules of engagement and the global response to conflicts that disproportionately affect civilian populations, particularly children.",
